      "model_output": {
        "actions": [],
        "on_topic": true,
        "reply": "They're named for the note they mark!\n\n**Treble clef = G clef.** Its swirl curls around the 2nd line from the bottom - that's G4, just above middle C. That G is your landmark, and you count the other lines and spaces out from it.\n\n**Bass clef = F clef.** Its two dots straddle the 4th line from the bottom - that's F3, just below middle C. Count out from that F.\n\nPut together they make the grand staff: bass staff on bottom, treble on top, with middle C (C4) sitting on a short ledger line in the middle between them.",
        "suggestions": [
